From: "mach-choice lane (C1)" <fleet@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] blazer: the R4/R5 always-on evidence chain (0123..0130) ported onto the blazer tree

Applies to the blazer integrated tree
(research/laguna-foundation/kernel-blazer/xnu-src/xnu-8796.121.2, branch hakios).
Ports the laguna-panic-capture lane's committed final state (kernel-wt @ 8d6d4b2:
0123 panic capture + 0124 hardening + 0129 XNU-MSGBUF mirror v1 + 0130 collision-free
window relocation) onto the platform-complete blazer mach.

Adaptations vs the 141 patches (all in-file, commented):
  1. laguna_panicdump.c body guard: #if defined(LAGUNA) -> #if defined(__arm64__) &&
     !defined(LAGUNA_PANICDUMP_STUB) — the BCM2837 build defines no LAGUNA, so the
     original guard silently compiles the stub path.
  2. arming site: LagunaKeyStore::start (141) -> MiniAppleKeyStore::start (blazer's
     first IOKit driver), extern "C" decl at file scope.
  3. bsd hooks use __arm64__ instead of ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_LAGUNA; arm_init anchors
     are arm_vm_init / serialmode (no laguna_early/dc9x00 calls exist there).
  4. start.s: PAN clear (.inst 0xd500409f) + bl EXT(laguna_logdump_entry) between
     DAIFSet and "mov x20, x0" in start_first_cpu (foundation has no pre-VBAR store
     of its own; the LGLW call needs x0 = boot_args PA).
  5. pe_init.c check_for_panic_log: second fallback arm for lagunapanicdump
     (default ON), reusing the existing blazer_panic_region .bss.
The tree's own opt-in hakios.blazer_panicdump (default OFF) is untouched — exactly
one default panic-capture writer. Boot args: lagunapanicdump=1/lagunalogdump=1 are
the defaults; =0 disables either; lagunapanictest=<sec> forces a validation panic.

Build proven on this host: make ... MACHINE_CONFIGS=BCM2837 KERNEL_CONFIGS=DEVELOPMENT
-j8 -k -> mach.development.bcm2837 sha256
b39179b5d0268c9c98432c46bda0cfda66eacce299efb1baf79899c5342f465b (16,416,856 B).

